#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Uvod"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmid; is &kde;'s &MIDI; and karaoke multimedia player. It offers some "
"features not found in any other &UNIX; &MIDI; player, such as real-time "
"graphics and karaoke text highlighting among others."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmid; currently runs on &Linux; only, but support for other operating "
"systems is planned, and hopefully will be available in the future. It uses "
"the <acronym>ALSA</acronym> sound driver, so it should run on every system "
"where &kde; and <acronym>ALSA</acronym> can compile."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmid; shows the lyrics in the main window, highlighting the words with a "
"different color while the music is playing, so it is very easy to follow the "
"songs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kmid;'s Features"
msgstr "&kmid; poboljšanja"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "These are some of &kmid;'s main features:"
msgstr "Osnovna &kmid; poboljšanja:"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It has a very <emphasis>friendly user interface</emphasis> to display "
"karaoke text with <emphasis>real-time highlighting</emphasis> of lyrics."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It features a graphical view of what is being played on each &MIDI; channel, "
"by highlighting the keys pressed in (virtual) piano keyboards."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The most powerful <emphasis>Midi Mapper</emphasis> that you will ever find "
"in any operating system."
msgstr ""
"Najjači <emphasis>Midi Mapper</emphasis> koji ćete pronaći na bilo kojem "
"operativnom sistemu."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Drag &amp; drop</emphasis> so you can drop in &kmid; any &MIDI; "
"file from a file manager like &konqueror; or &dolphin;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can <emphasis>change the tempo</emphasis> of songs to play them slower "
"or faster at your wish."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "It shows a visual metronome to easily follow the rhythm of the song."
msgstr "Prikazuje metronom da lakše pratite ritam pjesme."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "<emphasis>Customizable</emphasis> font and color for karaoke text."
msgstr "<emphasis>Prilagodiv</emphasis> font i boja teksta karaoke."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Supports the two standards used to include lyrics in &MIDI; files: lyrics "
"events and text events (guessing which one a song uses automatically)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Session Management. If a song is playing while you logout from &kde;, the "
"next time you login, the same song will start playing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid "<emphasis>Adjustable volume and pitch</emphasis> in real-time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid "It can play broken &MIDI; files which make other players core dump."
msgstr ""
"Može puštati oštećene &MIDI; fajlove koje drugi playeri ne mogu puštati."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Low <acronym>CPU</acronym> usage, depending on the complexity of the song."
msgstr ""
"Nisko iskorištenje <acronym>CPU</acronym>, zavisno od kompleksnosti pjesme."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid "Supports external &MIDI; synthesizers and software synths."
msgstr "Potržava eksterne &MIDI; sintisajzere i softver sintisajzer."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid "Runs on &Linux; with <acronym>ALSA</acronym> support."
msgstr "Pokreće se na  &Linux; sa<acronym>ALSA</acronym> podrškom."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid "General Usage"
msgstr "Opšta upotreba"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &MIDI;"
msgstr "Korištenje &MIDI;"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmid; outputs &MIDI; data, so it needs a &MIDI; receiver to render audible "
"sound. There are several kind of &MIDI; receivers, or Synthesizers, that you "
"can use. The only common required feature is <acronym>ALSA</acronym> &MIDI; "
"support."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid "External Devices"
msgstr "Eksterni uređaji"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These are peripheral devices, connected to the computer using a &MIDI; "
"cable. Modern devices may also include an <acronym>USB</acronym> interface. "
"The external &MIDI; devices are electronic musical instruments, that usually "
"can be played in standalone mode without requiring a connected computer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To connect a &MIDI; musical instrument to the computer, you need a &MIDI; "
"interface in the computer side and a &MIDI; cable. Some sound cards include "
"&MIDI; sockets, or cables. There are also cheap <acronym>USB</acronym> "
"&MIDI; interfaces. <acronym>ALSA</acronym> &MIDI; drivers are usually "
"available for them, and absolutely required for &kmid; usage."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If your &MIDI; musical instrument does not understand General &MIDI; "
"standard messages, you may need a &MIDI; map. See the <link linkend=\"MIDI-"
"maps\">&MIDI; Maps chapter</link> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sound Cards with a Hardware Synthesizer"
msgstr "Zvučna karica sa podrškom za Sintisajzerom"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These sound cards were very popular in the past, but much less common "
"nowadays. Some examples are the classic <acronym>GUS</acronym> and "
"<acronym>AWE</acronym> sound cards, or the SoundBlaster Audigy. All of them "
"are wave-table based synths. Even older are the FM synths, like the Ad Lib. "
"Anyway, they can render &MIDI; into audio in real-time, with the requirement "
"of <acronym>ALSA</acronym> &MIDI; drivers installed. For wave-table based "
"synths, it is also necessary a collection of sound samples, in the format "
"provided by the sound card manufacturer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid "Software Synthesizers"
msgstr "Softver sintisajzer"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since more <acronym>RAM</acronym> memory and <acronym>CPU</acronym> power is "
"available in modern computers, the number and usage of software synths is "
"growing quickly. It is also a cheap alternative, as the only required "
"hardware is a simple sound card, with only audio support. The integrated "
"audio device in many computer motherboards is adequate in most cases."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Two examples of applications capable of rendering &MIDI; data into audio "
"streams are &timidity; and &fluidsynth;. Both have <acronym>ALSA</acronym> "
"sequencer support, and are wave-table based synthesizers. There are options "
"in the <link linkend=\"configuration\">Configuration dialog</link> to launch "
"these soft synth programs automatically at startup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To use &timidity; you should install a <acronym>GUS</acronym> patches "
"collection, like freepats, or a &soundfont; file. You can start the program "
"in daemon mode, for instance using the timidity-daemon package in Debian "
"systems."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To use &fluidsynth; you should install a &soundfont; file. It may be a good "
"idea to install also the &qsynth; &GUI; front-end. Two excellent and free "
"sound fonts for &fluidsynth; are <ulink url=\"http://www.schristiancollins."
"com/soundfonts.php\">General User GS</ulink>, and Fluid R3, included in some "
"&Linux; distributions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opening Songs"
msgstr "Otvaranje pjesama"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can open a song in several different ways."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:279
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First, you can select <guimenuitem>Open...</guimenuitem> from the "
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> menu, then you are presented with a standard open "
"dialog, with which you can select the song you wish to open."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:285
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can drag a file from &konqueror; or &dolphin; and drop it into the "
"&kmid; window. You can also Drag &amp; Drop multiple songs at the same time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can specify one or more song file names in the command line when running "
"&kmid;. &URL; arguments are supported, so you can click and open a web link "
"or a file name in your file manager."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select a song from the list of recently played files, that are "
"displayed by the menu option <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Open Recent</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""
"Možete selektovati pjsmu sa liste nedavno puštanih fajlova, koje su "
"prikazane u meniju <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Open "
"Recent</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"And the final way is by selecting the song from the list of songs in the "
"active playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Anyway, the saved song settings from the last time you played the song are "
"automatically retrieved, if the option <menuchoice><guimenu>Song</"
"guimenu><guisubmenu>Song Settings</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Automatic</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> is enabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid "Playing Songs"
msgstr "Puštanje pjesama"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:319
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To play a song, first open it, and then press on the <guiicon>Play</guiicon> "
"button of the toolbar, choose the <guimenuitem>Play</guimenuitem> entry of "
"the <guimenu>Song</guimenu> menu, or just press the playback shortcut, by "
"default the <keycap>Media Play</keycap> key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that when you open a file, &kmid; will start playing it automatically. "
"This behavior can be disabled using the <guimenuitem>Auto-Start</"
"guimenuitem> option in the <guimenu>Song</guimenu> menu. If you drag and "
"drop more than one file, they will be added to a playlist and they will be "
"played sequentially."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:334
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once &kmid; is playing a song, you can move the time slider, by pressing "
"with the &MMB; mouse button, to go to a specified position."
msgstr ""
"Jednom kada  &kmid; svira pjesmu, moćete pomjerati klizač, pritiskom &MMB; "
"dugmeta na mišu, da odete na odabranu poziciju."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a song is playing too fast or too slow for you, you can use the tempo "
"slider. To get back to the default tempo, just press the \"100%\" button."
msgstr ""
"Ako se pjesma reprodukuje prebrzo ili presporo možete koristiti klizač za "
"temo. Da vratite podrazumjevani tempo samo pritisnite \"100%\" dugme."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:347
#, no-c-format
msgid "Displaying Lyrics"
msgstr "Prikazivanje teksta pjesme"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are two methods to store lyrics in a &MIDI; song file: by using "
"<guimenuitem>Text events</guimenuitem> or <guimenuitem>Lyrics events</"
"guimenuitem>. Some songs use the first method, some the second, both of "
"them, or none at all when the song does not include lyrics. &kmid; "
"automatically selects the most appropriate method for each song."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The SMF standard specification allows only ASCII text to be embedded inside "
"a &MIDI; file. However, you can find many &MIDI; files with texts encoded in "
"different ways. The text encoding of the lyrics can be selected using a "
"combo box located in the main window. The selected encoding will remain "
"until some other encoding is chosen, and will be remembered for the next "
"session."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:370
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuration Dialog"
msgstr "Konfiguracijski dijalog"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:372
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To open the <guilabel>Configure</guilabel> dialog, you can use the menu "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure &kmid;...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>, or the corresponding toolbar icon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The settings take effect as usual when you press the <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton> or <guibutton>Apply</guibutton> buttons."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lyrics Settings"
msgstr "Postavke stihova"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Font face</guilabel>. Here you can set the typography used to show "
"the song lyrics in the main window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Font color</guilabel>. This is the color used for the song text "
"when it has been already played."
msgstr ""
"<guilabel>Boja finta</guilabel>. Ovo je boja korištena za tekst pjesme koja "
"je već reprodukovana."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Font size</guilabel>. Here you can set the font size for the song "
"lyrics in the main window."
msgstr ""
"<guilabel>Veličina fonta</guilabel>. Ovdje moćete postaviti veličinu fonta "
"za tekst pjesme u glavnom prozoru."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:409
#, no-c-format
msgid "&MIDI; Settings"
msgstr "&MIDI; Postavke"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:412
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Output &MIDI; Connection</guilabel>. This list shows the available "
"&MIDI; connections detected in your system, as reported by the native &MIDI; "
"subsystem of your operating system. You should choose one of them, that will "
"be connected to the program's &MIDI; output port."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Show advanced &MIDI; ports</guilabel>. The advanced &MIDI; ports "
"are seldom used &MIDI; devices that are filtered out from the list of "
"available &MIDI; connections unless you select this checkbox."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:428
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>&MIDI; mapper file</guilabel>. Here you can choose the &MIDI; "
"mapper file that will be used with your external &MIDI; synthesizer. You can "
"find more information about &MIDI; mappers in the <link linkend=\"MIDI-maps"
"\">&MIDI; Maps chapter</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:436
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Reset Mode</guilabel>. This &MIDI; message is optionally sent to "
"the connected &MIDI; output port before starting to play each song, "
"resetting several parameters that could be changed by the last song file. "
"Here you can choose a standard message type recognized by your synthesizer, "
"or a custom system exclusive file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:448
#, no-c-format
msgid "Soft-Synths Settings"
msgstr "Postavke soft-sintisajzera"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:451
#, no-c-format
msgid "&fluidsynth;"
msgstr "&fluidsynth;"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:455
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Run &fluidsynth; at startup</guilabel>. If you select this "
"checkbox, the &fluidsynth; soft synth will be automatically launched at "
"startup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:461 index.docbook:512
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Command</guilabel>. Here you must set the path and name of the "
"soft synth command. Below this text box there is a label reporting the "
"detected program version, and an icon indicating if the minimal requirements "
"to use this program are met."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:469 index.docbook:520
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Audio Output</guilabel>. You should choose here the audio system "
"that will be used by the soft synth program."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:475 index.docbook:526
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Audio Device</guilabel>. Here you can specify an audio device name "
"for the soft synth output. It is usually safe to leave this setting blank."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:481 index.docbook:532
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Sample Rate</guilabel>. Here you can specify the audio sampling "
"rate used by the soft synth to generate digital audio. It is usually safe to "
"leave this setting blank."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:488
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Sound Font</guilabel>. Here you must set the path and file name of "
"the &soundfont; used by the soft synth. This argument is mandatory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:494 index.docbook:539
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Arguments</guilabel>. Here you can specify other optional "
"arguments that may be used with your soft synth. It is usual to leave it "
"blank."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:503
#, no-c-format
msgid "&timidity;"
msgstr "&timidity;"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:506
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Run &timidity; at startup</guilabel>. If you select this checkbox, "
"the &timidity; soft synth will be automatically launched at startup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:551
#, no-c-format
msgid "Playlists"
msgstr "Liste za reprodukciju"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:553
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A playlist is a list of &MIDI; files that you put in a set, and which are "
"played one after another. This section will help you to use them, and will "
"give you some useful tips to make a good use of them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:560
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating a Playlist"
msgstr "Kreiranje liste za reprodukciju"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:562
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To create a playlist, first open the <guilabel>Manage Playlist</guilabel> "
"dialog, by selecting the <guimenuitem>Edit Playlist...</guimenuitem> entry "
"of the <guimenu>Playlist</guimenu> menu, and add your files to the playlist. "
"Finally, select the <guimenuitem>Save Playlist...</guimenuitem> entry of the "
"<guimenu>Playlist</guimenu> menu, and provide the folder and file name for "
"your playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:571
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The playlist file is a simple text file that you can edit, copy and move "
"using your usual file management tools."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:579
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding Songs to a Playlist"
msgstr "Dodavanje pjesama u listu za reprodukciju"

#. Tag: subtitle
#: index.docbook:580
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to Use <guimenuitem>Auto-Add to Playlist</guimenuitem> Menu Option"
msgstr ""
"Kako koristiti <guimenuitem>Automatsko dodavanje u listu za reprodukciju </"
"guimenuitem> opciju menija"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:583
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If <guimenuitem>Auto-Add to Playlist</guimenuitem> is enabled, when you open "
"a song (using <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Open...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> or Drag &amp; Drop) it (they) will be added to the "
"active playlist without user intervention."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:590
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If <guimenuitem>Auto-Add to Playlist</guimenuitem> is not enabled, when you "
"open a song a temporary playlist will be created and cleared, and the opened "
"songs will be added to it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:599
#, no-c-format
msgid "Removing Songs from Playlists"
msgstr "Uklanjanje pjesama iz liste za reprodukciju"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:601
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To delete a song from a playlist, just open the <guilabel>Manage Playlist</"
"guilabel> dialog, select the song you wish to delete, and then click on the "
"<guibutton>Remove</guibutton> button, pressing finally the <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton> button to close the dialog window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:611
#, no-c-format
msgid "Playing Order"
msgstr "Red puštanja"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:613
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The songs are played in the same order they are set in the playlist. You can "
"edit the order of the songs using the <guilabel>Manage Playlist</guilabel> "
"dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:619
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenuitem>Repeat</guimenuitem> mode loops the playlist, repeating the "
"first song again when the last song has finished."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:624
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you select the <guimenuitem>Shuffle</guimenuitem> mode, &kmid; will "
"randomize the order of the songs in the playlist. The playlist will be "
"shuffled each time you add a new file in the active playlist, and when you "
"activate the <guimenuitem>Shuffle</guimenuitem> mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:634
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selecting a Song from a Playlist"
msgstr "Selektovanje pjesme iz liste za reprodukciju"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:636
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select a song among the songs of the playlist using the "
"<guilabel>Manage Playlist</guilabel> dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:641
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also change to the next song by using the <guimenuitem>Next Song</"
"guimenuitem> entry of the <guimenu>Song</guimenu> menu, the <guilabel>Next "
"Song</guilabel> button of the toolbar, or pressing the user configured "
"shortcut key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:648
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change to the previous song, use the <guimenuitem>Previous Song</"
"guimenuitem> entry of the <guimenu>Song</guimenu> menu, the "
"<guimenuitem>Previous Song</guimenuitem> button of the toolbar, or press the "
"user configured shortcut key."
msgstr ""
"Da promjenite prethodnu pjesmu koristite <guimenuitem>Previous Song</"
"guimenuitem>iz  <guimenu>Song</guimenu> menija, <guimenuitem>Previous Song</"
"guimenuitem> dugme iz toolbara, ili pritisnite kraticu za to na tastaturi."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:658
#, no-c-format
msgid "Deleting a Playlist"
msgstr "Brisanje liste za reprodukciju"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:660
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To delete the contents of a playlist, simply open the <guilabel>Manage "
"Playlist</guilabel> dialog and click the <guibutton>Reset</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""
"Da obrišete sadržaj iz liste za reprodukciju jednostano otvorite "
"<guilabel>Upravljaj listom izvođenja</guilabel> dijalog i kliknite "
"<guibutton>Reset</guibutton> dugme."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:665
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To delete a playlist file stored on disk, use your favorite file management "
"tool."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:674
#, no-c-format
msgid "&MIDI; Maps"
msgstr "&MIDI; Mape"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:677
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is a &MIDI; Map ?"
msgstr "Šta je &MIDI; Mapa ?"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:679
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A &MIDI; map is something that maps &MIDI; events in other &MIDI; events."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:684
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is totally needed if a synthesizer does not understand the standard "
"events (that is, if a synthesizer is not General &MIDI; compliant), in this "
"case, a &MIDI; map will translate General &MIDI; events in the events that "
"the synthesizer understands."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:691
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For example you can make a &MIDI; map that converts all the <literal>Change "
"patch to Bright Piano</literal> events, to <literal>Change patch to Trumpet</"
"literal> events, and so when a song tries to play a piano, it will play a "
"trumpet instead."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:698
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This may sound odd, (why playing a trumpet when the song is made to play a "
"piano?), but it is very useful. The <acronym>GM</acronym> standard specifies "
"that when a &MIDI; keyboard receives a patch change event to <literal>0</"
"literal>, it will change the current patch to <literal>Grand Piano</"
"literal>, but an older synthesizer will change for example to a "
"<literal>Electric Guitar</literal> when it receives a <literal>0</literal>. "
"This old keyboard, needed to receive a <literal>3</literal> (for example) to "
"change to a <literal>Piano</literal>. And here comes the &MIDI; map in "
"action, changing all <literal>change patch to 0</literal> to <literal>change "
"patch to 3</literal> and thus really playing the correct instrument when it "
"has to."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:716
#, no-c-format
msgid "Do I Need a &MIDI; Map ?"
msgstr "Da li mi je potreba &MIDI; Mapa?"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:718
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In short, if you do not have an external synth, the answer is <emphasis>no</"
"emphasis>."
msgstr ""
"Ukratno, ako nemate eksterni sintisajzer, odgovor je <emphasis>no</emphasis>."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:722
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you only have a sound card with &MIDI; synth, &MIDI; maps are not likely "
"needed because almost all the sound cards are <acronym>GM</acronym> "
"compliant (this include AWE cards, <acronym>GUS</acronym> cards, "
"<acronym>FM</acronym> devices and so on)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:729
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are playing music through an external synthesizer, and it is not GM "
"compliant, you will need to make a &MIDI; map for your &MIDI; device. "
"Although you will perhaps spend a whole afternoon doing your map file and "
"trying different values for all the options, you will be fully rewarded when "
"you finish it, because you will be able to correctly listen many song files "
"that would sound wrong otherwise."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:741
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating a &MIDI; Map"
msgstr "Kreiranje &MIDI; Mape"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:743
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is not any program to generate &MIDI; maps, so you will have to edit a "
"file by hand (using your favorite text editor)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:748
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A Midi map is a text file that keeps all the needed translations there will "
"be made when playing music."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:753
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It consist of four sections: <literal>PATCHMAP</literal>, <literal>KEYMAP</"
"literal>, <literal>CHANNELMAP</literal> and <literal>OPTIONS</literal>. Each "
"section must appear only once."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:760
#, no-c-format
msgid "The general structure of a map file is an ini style file:"
msgstr "Generalna struktura mape je kao:"

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:764
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[PATCHMAP]\n"
"...\n"
"\n"
"# comment line\n"
" \n"
"[KEYMAP]\n"
"...\n"
"\n"
"[CHANNELMAP]\n"
"...\n"
"\n"
"[OPTIONS]\n"
"..."
msgstr ""
"[PATCHMAP]\n"
"...\n"
"\n"
"# comment line\n"
" \n"
"[KEYMAP]\n"
"...\n"
"\n"
"[CHANNELMAP]\n"
"...\n"
"\n"
"[OPTIONS]\n"
"..."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:766
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each one of the four section names between square brackets starts the "
"corresponding section. You can put comments by starting the line with a "
"<literal>&num;</literal> character. Each section is a collection of several "
"lines of key=value pairs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:773
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please, do not forget to send me your map file by email, so that future "
"releases of &kmid; will include support for more non General Midi compliant "
"keyboards."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:780
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <literal>PATCHMAP</literal> Section"
msgstr "<literal>PATCHMAP</literal> odjeljak"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:782
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section is used to specify how patches are going to be mapped, from GM "
"to your keyboard specs. The general usage is:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:787
#, no-c-format
msgid "(Name of GM Patch name)=(<replaceable>N</replaceable>)"
msgstr "(Ime GM Patch imena)=(<replaceable>N</replaceable>)"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:789
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Where <replaceable>N</replaceable> is the number that you keyboard needs to "
"receive to change the patch to the same that the GM standard does ."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:794
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please note that the left side of the equal sign is a symbolic key, so you "
"can change the order of the lines and omit any of the 128 instruments."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:802
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <literal>KEYMAP</literal> Section"
msgstr "<literal>KEYMAP</literal> odjeljak"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:804
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <literal>KEYMAP</literal> section is used to specify how percussion keys "
"are going to be mapped. The usage is:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:809
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[KEYMAP]\n"
"C 0 =0\n"
"C#0 =1\n"
"D 0 =2\n"
"..."
msgstr ""
"[KEYMAP]\n"
"C 0 =0\n"
"C#0 =1\n"
"D 0 =2\n"
"..."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:811
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As with the <literal>PATCHMAP</literal> section, you can change the order of "
"the lines, and omit any of them. Only the first four characters of each key "
"are taken into account."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:817
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Keymaps are only used to map keys in the percussion channel. Have a look at "
"the distributed maps to see some examples."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:825
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <literal>CHANNELMAP</literal> Section"
msgstr "<literal>CHANNELMAP</literal> odjeljak"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:827
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section can be used to map some channels to different ones. For "
"example, if you want to swap the first and second channels, you can easily "
"do it within the <literal>CHANNELMAP</literal> section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:833
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"However it is more useful for keyboards that need the percussion channel to "
"be in a given channel (the GM standard use the channel 10, others use the "
"channel 16 and others use channel 9)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:839
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that &MIDI; devices use 16 channels, so the <literal>CHANNELMAP</"
"literal> section, has 16 lines, from 0 to 15 , as this one:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:844
#, no-c-format
msgid "(N) = (M)"
msgstr "(N) = (M)"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:846
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Where <literal>N</literal> is the channel which is mapped to the <literal>M</"
"literal> channel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:854
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <literal>OPTIONS</literal> Section"
msgstr "<literal>OPTIONS</literal> odjeljak"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:856
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <literal>OPTIONS</literal> section has some general options that can be "
"very useful:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:861
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[OPTIONS]\n"
"PitchBenderRatio = r\n"
"MapExpressionToVolumeEvents = true\n"
"ForceDrumsPatch = 30"
msgstr ""
"[OPTIONS]\n"
"PitchBenderRatio = r\n"
"MapExpressionToVolumeEvents = true\n"
"ForceDrumsPatch = 30"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:863
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can specify all options, only one, or none of them."
msgstr "Možete navesti sve opcije, samo jedno ili ni jednu."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:867
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <literal>PitchBenderRatio r</literal> value, has the ratio by which "
"pitch bender events will be multiplied. That is, when a &MIDI; file tries to "
"send a pitch bender event with a <literal>n</literal> value, the real value "
"that will be sent is <literal>n*(r/4096)</literal> (the <literal>4096</"
"literal> value is for not having to put decimal points in the map file)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:876
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is used because the <acronym>GM</acronym> standard says that when a "
"&MIDI; keyboard receives a Pitch Bender event with a 4096 data value, it "
"should bend the note to a higher one , but some &MIDI; keyboards try to bend "
"the initial note by two or more higher notes (even an octave higher!) when "
"they receive a 4096. This can be easily fixed by trying different values so "
"that instead of sending a 4096, &kmid; sends the appropriate value."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:886
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the <literal>MapExpressionToVolumeEvents</literal> option is set in the "
"map file, and a &MIDI; file try to send an expression event, &kmid; will "
"send a volume event which is understood by more non-GM keyboards, and which "
"has a similar effect. There are many &MIDI; files which use expression "
"events to fade out at the end of a song, so if you feel that music should be "
"heard softer and softer, you can turn on this option and see if this is what "
"you need, because your &MIDI; synthesizer could be ignoring the expression "
"events because it does not understand them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:897
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <literal>ForceDrumsPatch</literal> option may be useful to always use "
"the percussion patch on the percussion channel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:907
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &MIDI; Maps"
msgstr "Korištenje &MIDI; Mapa"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:909
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To use a &MIDI; map, open the <guilabel>Configuration</guilabel> dialog by "
"selecting the <guimenuitem>Configure &kmid;...</guimenuitem> entry of the "
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:915
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then click the <guilabel>&MIDI;</guilabel> category icon, and select the map "
"file in the <guilabel>&MIDI; mapper file</guilabel> combo box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:924
#, no-c-format
msgid "Advanced Features"
msgstr "Naprijedne funkcije"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:927
#, no-c-format
msgid "Song Settings"
msgstr "Postavke pjesama"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:928
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For each played song, several options can be saved and automatically "
"retrieved the next time the song is opened. These options are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:931
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text encoding"
msgstr "Kodiranje teksta"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:932
#, no-c-format
msgid "Volume"
msgstr "Jačina zvuka"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:933
#, no-c-format
msgid "Pitch (tone, transposition)"
msgstr "Teren (ton, transpozicija)"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:934
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rhythm tempo"
msgstr "Tempo ritma"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:935
#, no-c-format
msgid "Channel labels"
msgstr "Labela kanala"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:936
#, no-c-format
msgid "Channel buttons"
msgstr "Dugmad kanala"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:937
#, no-c-format
msgid "Channel instruments"
msgstr "Instrumenti kanala"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:941
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you do not want automatic saving and retrieving, you can use the "
"<guimenuitem>Load</guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem>Save</guimenuitem> menu "
"options available in the menu <menuchoice><guimenu>Song</guimenu> "
"<guisubmenu>Song Settings</guisubmenu></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:950
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Channel View"
msgstr "Pregled kanala"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:952
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Channel view is a table of 16 rows, one for each &MIDI; channel. In each "
"row there is a text box where you can label the channels for your own "
"reference, buttons to enable the <guilabel>Solo</guilabel> and "
"<guilabel>Mute</guilabel> functions, a vu-meter, and also a <guilabel>Lock</"
"guilabel> button and a combo box where you can see and change the musical "
"instrument for each channel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:961
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Only the active channels (the channels used by the current song) have "
"enabled controls."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:968
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Piano Player view"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:970
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Piano Player view can show up to 16 virtual keyboards, one for each "
"&MIDI; channel. Only the active channels (the channels used by the current "
"song) can be enabled. The virtual keyboards not only show the played notes "
"in real-time, but can be used also to trigger notes using the mouse or the "
"computer keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:981
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Rhythm Controls"
msgstr "Kontrole ritma"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:983
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The rhythm controls are: a tempo label, showing the song tempo in beats per "
"minute, a visual metronome including a measure/part counter, and a tempo "
"slider to modify the song tempo, that is, the speed of the song."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:989
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you changed the tempo, you can get back the original one clicking on the "
"<guilabel>100%</guilabel> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:999
#, no-c-format
msgid "Key Bindings"
msgstr "Veze tastera"

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:1005
#, no-c-format
msgid "<entry>Key</entry>"
msgstr "<entry>Taster</entry>"

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:1006
#, no-c-format
msgid "Action"
msgstr "Aktivnost"

#. Tag: keysym
#: index.docbook:1011
#, no-c-format
msgid "Media Play"
msgstr "Medijsko emitovanje"

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:1012
#, no-c-format
msgid "Play the loaded song."
msgstr "Pusti učitanu pjesmu."

#. Tag: keysym
#: index.docbook:1015
#, no-c-format
msgid "Media Stop"
msgstr "Stopiranje medije"

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:1016
#, no-c-format
msgid "Stop playing"
msgstr "Zaustavi izvođenje"

#. Tag: keycombo
#: index.docbook:1019
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Ctrl;<keycap>Q</keycap>"
msgstr "&Ctrl;<keycap>Q</keycap>"

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:1020
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quit &kmid;"
msgstr "Napusti &kmid;"

#. Tag: keycap
#: index.docbook:1023
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keycap>F1</keycap>"
msgstr "<keycap>F1</keycap>"

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:1024
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open this document"
msgstr "Otvori ovaj dokument"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1033
#, no-c-format
msgid "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)"
msgstr "Često postavljena pitanja (FAQ)"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1038
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is exactly a &MIDI; file?"
msgstr "Šta je ustvari &MIDI; fajl?"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1044
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A Midi file contains information about how to play a song, that is, it "
"contains the notes, the rhythm, velocity, &etc; This implies that the same "
"&MIDI; file, when played in two different devices can produce very different "
"results. It is like a musical score, that can be performed very differently "
"by two different musicians."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1055
#, no-c-format
msgid "I can get better sound with a mp3/wav player, why should I use &kmid;?"
msgstr ""
"Kada mogu imati bolju kvalitetu zvuka sa mp3/wav plajerom, zašto bih "
"koristio &kmid;?"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1060
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The size of a typical &MIDI; file is about 50 KB. while the typical mp3 "
"filesize is 4 MB. And with a good synthesizer device, you can get a "
"comparable sound quality. Even more, with a &MIDI; file, you can change "
"individual instruments, change the velocity of a song, &etc; so you have "
"more overall control."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1067
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Another point of view about this: comparing &MIDI; and mp3 is like comparing "
"painting with photography. Or comparing <acronym>SVG</acronym> with jpeg. "
"Each one has different properties and use cases."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1077
#, no-c-format
msgid "I cannot get my sound card to work with &kmid;, what can I do?"
msgstr "Moja zvućna kartica nem može raditi sa &kmid;, šta da radim?"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1082
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First, you should verify your ALSA installation and configuration. Second, "
"you need to connect &kmid; to a &MIDI; synthesizer. If your sound card does "
"not have one, use a software synth instead."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1092
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I want to add a whole folder to a playlist, but having to add the &MIDI; "
"files one by one is not funny."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1098
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I agree, that's why &kmid; supports Drag &amp; Drop. Just open, in "
"&konqueror; or &dolphin;, the folder you want to add, select all the files, "
"drag them and drop them in &kmid;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Be sure to set the <guimenuitem>Auto-Add to Playlist</guimenuitem> option "
"before, so that the files will be added to the current playlist. If you do "
"not do this, files will be added to a new temporary playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1113
#, no-c-format
msgid "I cannot follow the lyrics, it's playing too fast!"
msgstr "Ne mogu pratiti tekst, reprodukuje se prebrzo!"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use the rhythm control tempo slider to make it play slower. Remember "
"that you can press the <guilabel>100%</guilabel> button to restore the "
"original tempo."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1130
#, no-c-format
msgid "Final Notes"
msgstr "Konačne bilješke"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1133
#, no-c-format
msgid "Some Tips and Tricks"
msgstr "Neki savjeti i trikovi"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I will include some tips so that you can take fully advantage from all the "
"features of &kmid;:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:1142
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opening files"
msgstr "Otvaranje fajlova"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1144
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I always keep a &kde; desktop with a &konqueror; or &dolphin; window in my "
"root &MIDI; folder, and &kmid; in this desktop (if playing a &MIDI; file) or "
"sticky (if playing a karaoke file :-)). This way, when the active playlist "
"finishes, or I want to play some file, I just go to the &konqueror; or "
"&dolphin; window, select the desired files and Drag &amp; Drop to the "
"&kmid;'s window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1152
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Suppose that you want to play some &MIDI; files, but do not want to add them "
"to any playlist, well, just turn off the <guimenuitem>Auto-Add to Playlist</"
"guimenuitem> option in the <guimenu>Playlist</guimenu> menu, and open the "
"files, they will be added to a temporary playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:1162
#, no-c-format
msgid "Another method to create a new playlist"
msgstr "Druge metode da kreirate novu listu za reprodukciju"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1164
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Suppose that you have &MIDI; files <filename>A.mid</filename>, <filename>B."
"mid</filename> and <filename>C.mid</filename>. At first you only want to "
"play the first &MIDI; file, so you unselect <guimenuitem>Auto-Add</"
"guimenuitem> and open <filename>A.mid</filename>. You get then a Temporary "
"playlist with only one &MIDI; file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then you decide to play also B and C, and make a playlist with all them, "
"what do you do?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Easy, select <guimenuitem>Auto-Add</guimenuitem> and open <filename>B.mid</"
"filename> and <filename>C.mid</filename> (by any of the multiple methods), "
"they will be automatically added to the temporary playlist, that will then "
"have <filename>A.mid</filename>, <filename>B.mid</filename> and <filename>C."
"mid</filename>. At this point, you can use the <guimenuitem>Save Playlist</"
"guimenuitem> dialog, enter the name of the new playlist, and you are done. "
"You already have a new playlist, which holds the A, B and C &MIDI; files, "
"and that is not deleted when you close &kmid;."
msgstr ""

